---
import CourseOverview from '../components/CourseOverview.astro';
import HomeLayout from '../layouts/HomeLayout.astro';
import { chapters, chapterPreviews, v2Chapters } from '../data/chapters';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const archivedPageCount = chapters.length + chapterPreviews.length + v2Chapters.length;
---

<HomeLayout
  title="The New Engineering Paradigm"
  description="Why engineering is changing: higher expectations, shorter feedback cycles, software-inspired workflows and AI-assisted engineering across disciplines."
>
  <section class="opening" aria-labelledby="page-title">
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">Engineering transformation · Software-driven practices · AI</p>
      <h1 id="page-title">Engineering must evolve. <br /><span>So must how we engineer.</span></h1>
      <p class="deck">Markets expect shorter development cycles, more frequent improvements and higher quality. Software-inspired practices are spreading across electronics, physical products and systems engineering; AI introduces new ways to explore, implement and evaluate changes. This course asks how teams might deliver useful changes faster and at lower cost while maintaining evidence about the whole product.</p>
      <p class="principle">We build the machine that builds the machine: improve the engineering environment alongside the product.</p>
    </div>
    <aside class="destination" aria-label="The engineering question">
      <p class="label">Two entry points</p>
      <p>Start with <a href={`${base}learn/v3/01-the-new-engineering-paradigm/`}>Chapter 1</a> for the executive overview, then <a href={`${base}learn/v3/02-introducing-the-engineering-challenge/`}>Chapter 2</a> to meet the fictional intersection case used throughout the course.</p>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="approach" id="approach" aria-labelledby="approach-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <h2 id="approach-title">Develop the system. <br />Develop how we engineer it.</h2>
      <span class="small-label">Conceptual approach</span>
    </div>
    <figure aria-labelledby="approach-title" aria-describedby="approach-caption">
      <div class="connected-systems">
        <div class="cycle product-cycle">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 320 260" aria-hidden="true">
            <defs><marker id="product-arrow" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="6" refY="4" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0L8 4L0 8" fill="var(--home-teal)" /></marker></defs>
            <path class="cycle-arc" d="M143 40C77 40 38 109 77 181" marker-end="url(#product-arrow)" />
            <path class="cycle-arc" d="M91 200C122 226 190 226 225 200" marker-end="url(#product-arrow)" />
            <path class="cycle-arc" d="M241 182C275 120 250 48 178 40" marker-end="url(#product-arrow)" />
          </svg>
          <div class="cycle-centre">
            <p class="cycle-name">Product system</p>
            <p class="cycle-detail">Software · electronics<br />Physical design · AI</p>
          </div>
          <p class="cycle-node node-top">Understand use</p>
          <p class="cycle-node node-left">Model<br />and experiment</p>
          <p class="cycle-node node-right">Integrate<br />and validate</p>
        </div>
        <div class="decision-hub">
          <p class="flow-label">New product ambitions<br />change the engineering work <span class="forward" aria-hidden="true">→</span></p>
          <p class="decision">Decide what to test<br />and what to build next.</p>
          <p class="flow-label"><span class="return" aria-hidden="true">←</span>New engineering capabilities<br />expand what we can try</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cycle environment-cycle">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 320 260" aria-hidden="true">
            <defs><marker id="environment-arrow" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="6" refY="4" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0L8 4L0 8" fill="var(--home-gold)" /></marker></defs>
            <g transform="rotate(90 160 130)">
              <path class="cycle-arc" d="M143 40C77 40 38 109 77 181" marker-end="url(#environment-arrow)" />
              <path class="cycle-arc" d="M91 200C122 226 190 226 225 200" marker-end="url(#environment-arrow)" />
              <path class="cycle-arc" d="M241 182C275 120 250 48 178 40" marker-end="url(#environment-arrow)" />
            </g>
          </svg>
          <div class="cycle-centre">
            <p class="cycle-name">Engineering<br />environment</p>
            <p class="cycle-detail">People · models<br />Tools · AI agents</p>
          </div>
          <p class="cycle-node node-top">Develop methods and models</p>
          <p class="cycle-node node-left">Work with<br />AI agents</p>
          <p class="cycle-node node-right">Automate<br />and evaluate</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="shared-thread">
        <p class="label">Executable engineering</p>
        <p>Executable models make behavior testable. Automated checks give AI agents actionable feedback: propose a change, execute it, inspect the result and improve it within agreed boundaries. Engineers determine whether the model and its checks are suitable for the product question.</p>
      </div>
      <figcaption id="approach-caption">We build the machine that builds the machine.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="example" aria-labelledby="example-title">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <h2 id="example-title">The recurring engineering challenge starts in Chapter 2.</h2>
      <span class="small-label">Conceptual workflow</span>
    </div>
    <p class="example-question">A fictional city considers improving a four-way intersection. First we establish stakeholders, system boundaries and uncertainty; later we use a bounded fixed-phase model to test one specific question. <a href={`${base}learn/v3/02-introducing-the-engineering-challenge/`}>Read the introduction to the example.</a></p>
    <div class="example-thread">
      <div class="example-step">
        <p class="label">Define + model</p>
        <h3>Frame the whole-system problem.</h3>
        <p>Clarify the needs of drivers, pedestrians, operators and maintainers before selecting a preferred solution or model.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="example-step observed">
        <span class="step-connector" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        <p class="label">Execute + evaluate</p>
        <h3>Investigate with bounded models.</h3>
        <p>Use controlled scenarios and tests to explore alternatives. AI agents may help refine bounded changes where independent automated checks provide meaningful feedback.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="example-step next-work">
        <span class="step-connector" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        <p class="label">Interpret + decide</p>
        <h3>Integrate, verify and release responsibly.</h3>
        <p>Connect software evidence with electronics, physical interfaces, operational needs and release authority. An executable model is not a qualified controller.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="example-caption">The example is fictional. Fast automated feedback supports learning and agentic iteration; whole-product evidence determines which results are actually relevant to integration and release.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="notes">
    <section class="note" aria-labelledby="collaboration-title">
      <p class="note-number">01 / Modelling and exploration</p>
      <h2 id="collaboration-title">Make ideas<br />executable.</h2>
      <p>Use software models, simulations and physical prototypes to examine specific engineering questions. Deterministic calculations have predictable results for defined inputs; experiments reveal what changes when conditions or designs change.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="note" aria-labelledby="progress-title">
      <p class="note-number">02 / Teams and workflows</p>
      <h2 id="progress-title">Engineer the<br />feedback loop.</h2>
      <p>Design automated behavioral and integration checks that tell agents what failed and why. Let them refine bounded changes, while preserving independent criteria and making demonstrated behavior—not generated output—the measure of progress.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="note" aria-labelledby="feedback-title">
      <p class="note-number">03 / Release and feedback</p>
      <h2 id="feedback-title">Check against<br />reality.</h2>
      <p>Automated tests support fast inner loops. Product validity, physical interfaces, operational conditions and release authority form a broader loop with different evidence and cadences. A green test suite cannot answer every product question.</p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <CourseOverview />

  <section class="more-reading" aria-labelledby="resources-title">
    <header>
      <p class="label">Go further</p>
      <h2 id="resources-title">Explore the lab.</h2>
    </header>
    <div class="resource-links">
      <article class="companion-reading">
        <p class="label">Bonus reading</p>
        <h3><a href={`${base}bonus/building-the-machine-that-builds-the-machine/`}>Building the Machine That Builds the Machine <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></h3>
        <p>When does it pay to invest in the environment you use to engineer a product? Follow the decision from a small documentation project to an engineering team.</p>
      </article>
      <ul class="resource-routes">
        <li><a href={`${base}lab/`}><span class="label">Lab</span><span class="resource-title">Try the coverage model <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span><span class="resource-description">Move the sensor or change its radius, then compare the calculated coverage.</span></a></li>
        <li><a href={`${base}reference/`}><span class="label">Reference</span><span class="resource-title">Explore the engineering sources <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span><span class="resource-description">Find definitions, model assumptions and the evidence behind the examples.</span></a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="archive" aria-labelledby="reading-title">
    <details class="course-directory" id="published-lessons">
      <summary id="reading-title"><span class="label">Archive</span>{' '}Earlier courses and experiments <span class="archive-count">{archivedPageCount} pages</span></summary>
      <div class="directory-content">
        <h3 id="published-v2">Earlier previews and articles</h3>
        <ul class="article-list">
          {chapterPreviews.map(chapter => <li><a href={`${base}learn/${chapter.path}/`}>{chapter.title} <span class="archive-kind">V2 reader preview</span></a></li>)}
          {v2Chapters.map(chapter => <li><a href={`${base}learn/${chapter.path}/`}>{chapter.title} <span class="archive-kind">V2 article</span></a></li>)}
        </ul>
        <h3>Original single-sensor course</h3>
        <ol id="learning-path" class="lesson-list">
          {chapters.map(chapter => <li><a href={`${base}learn/${chapter.path}/`}>{chapter.title}</a></li>)}
        </ol>
        <a class="learning-path-link" href={`${base}learn/`}>Return to the current learning path <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>
</HomeLayout>

<style>
  .opening { position: relative; isolation: isolate; display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 2.4fr) minmax(0, 1fr); align-items: end; gap: 3rem; padding-block: 2.875rem 2.625rem; }
  .opening::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: -1;
    pointer-events: none;
    background-image: url('../assets/hero-hexagons.svg');
    background-size: 3rem 5.19615rem;
    mask-image: radial-gradient(ellipse 80% 85% at 75% 25%, #000, transparent 75%);
  }
  .kicker, .label, .small-label, .note-number { font-family: var(--home-mono); font-size: .6875rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .kicker, .label, .note-number { color: var(--home-gold); text-transform: uppercase; }
  .kicker { letter-spacing: .0625rem; margin-bottom: 1.1875rem; color: var(--home-teal); }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(2.125rem, 4.6vw, 3.375rem); font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.08; letter-spacing: -.115rem; text-wrap: balance; }
  h1 span { color: var(--home-gold); }
  .deck, .principle { font-size: .9375rem; line-height: 1.75; max-width: 43rem; }
  .deck { color: var(--home-muted); margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .principle { margin-top: 1.125rem; }
  .destination { border-left: 1px solid #677274; padding-left: 1.25rem; color: var(--home-muted); font-size: .875rem; line-height: 1.75; margin-bottom: .25rem; }
  .destination .label { color: var(--home-text); margin-bottom: .75rem; letter-spacing: .0625rem; }
  .approach { border-top: 1px solid var(--home-rule); padding-block: 1.875rem 2.5rem; }
  .section-heading { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1.5rem; }
  .section-heading h2 { font-size: 1.75rem; line-height: 1.25; letter-spacing: -.05rem; font-weight: 500; }
  .small-label { color: var(--home-muted); }
  .connected-systems { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 13.125rem minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 1.5rem; align-items: center; margin-block: 1.75rem 1.5rem; }
  .cycle { position: relative; height: 16.25rem; width: 100%; max-width: 24rem; margin-inline: auto; }
  .cycle svg { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; }
  .cycle-arc { fill: none; stroke: var(--home-teal); stroke-width: 1.5; opacity: .8; }
  .environment-cycle .cycle-arc { stroke: var(--home-gold); }
  .cycle-centre { position: absolute; top: 50%; left: 10%; right: 10%; transform: translateY(-50%); text-align: center; }
  .cycle-name { color: var(--home-teal); font: .8125rem/1.6 var(--home-mono); letter-spacing: .055rem; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .environment-cycle .cycle-name { color: var(--home-gold); }
  .cycle-detail { font-size: .6875rem; line-height: 1.6; margin-top: .5rem; color: var(--home-muted); }
  .cycle-node { position: absolute; padding: .375rem .5rem; background: var(--home-bg); text-align: center; font-size: .8125rem; line-height: 1.45; }
  .node-top { top: 0; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); white-space: nowrap; }
  .node-left { left: 0; bottom: 0; }
  .node-right { right: 0; bottom: 0; }
  .decision-hub { text-align: center; }
  .decision { font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.4; background: var(--home-panel); padding: 1.125rem .75rem; border-top: 2px solid var(--home-teal); border-bottom: 2px solid var(--home-gold); }
  .flow-label { color: var(--home-muted); font-size: .6875rem; line-height: 1.5; padding-block: .75rem; }
  .flow-label span { display: block; font-size: 1.375rem; line-height: 1.3; }
  .forward { color: var(--home-teal); }
  .return { color: var(--home-gold); }
  .shared-thread { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 12rem 1fr; gap: 1.75rem; align-items: start; border-block: 1px solid var(--home-rule); padding-block: 1.125rem; }
  .shared-thread .label { color: var(--home-teal); letter-spacing: .03rem; }
  .shared-thread > p:last-child { font-size: .8125rem; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--home-muted); }
  figcaption { font-size: .875rem; line-height: 1.7; text-align: center; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .example { padding: 1.625rem; border: 1px solid var(--home-rule); background-color: var(--home-panel); background-image: linear-gradient(rgb(200 217 222 / 3%) 1px, transparent 1px), linear-gradient(90deg, rgb(200 217 222 / 3%) 1px, transparent 1px); background-size: 3rem 3rem; }
  .example .section-heading h2 { font-size: 1.4375rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .example-question { max-width: 55rem; margin-top: 1rem; color: var(--home-muted); font-size: .875rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  .example-thread { display: grid; grid-template-columns: .9fr 1.1fr 1.2fr; gap: 2.625rem; margin-top: 1.625rem; }
  .example-step { position: relative; }
  .example-step .label { margin-bottom: .625rem; }
  .example-step h3 { font-size: 1.125rem; line-height: 1.35; letter-spacing: -.025rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .example-step > p:not(.label) { font-size: .75rem; line-height: 1.75; margin-top: .75rem; color: var(--home-muted); }
  .example-step strong { font-weight: 500; color: var(--home-text); }
  .observed .label { color: var(--home-teal); }
  .step-connector { position: absolute; top: 2.125rem; left: -1.875rem; color: var(--home-muted); font-size: 1.25rem; }
  .example-caption { border-top: 1px solid var(--home-rule); padding-top: 1rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; font-size: .75rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--home-muted); }
  .notes { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1.75rem; padding-block: 2.125rem 2rem; }
  .note { border-top: 1px solid var(--home-rule); padding-top: 1.0625rem; }
  .note-number { letter-spacing: .025rem; margin-bottom: .75rem; }
  .note h2 { font-size: 1.375rem; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.25; letter-spacing: -.0375rem; }
  .note > p:last-child { font-size: .8125rem; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--home-muted); margin-top: .9375rem; }
  .more-reading { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 2.1fr; gap: 2rem; padding-block: 2rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--home-rule); }
  .more-reading > header > .label { color: var(--home-teal); margin-bottom: .625rem; }
  .more-reading h2 { font-size: 1.75rem; line-height: 1.25; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -.035em; }
  .companion-reading { padding-left: 1.25rem; border-left: 2px solid var(--home-gold); }
  .companion-reading > .label { color: var(--home-gold); }
  .companion-reading h3 { margin-top: .5rem; font-size: 1.1875rem; line-height: 1.45; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
  .companion-reading h3 a > span { color: var(--home-gold); }
  .companion-reading > p:last-child { margin-top: .75rem; color: var(--home-muted); font-size: .875rem; line-height: 1.75; }
  .resource-routes { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1.5rem; list-style: none; margin: 1.75rem 0 0; padding: 0; }
  .resource-routes a { display: flex; flex-direction: column; height: 100%; border-top: 1px solid var(--home-rule); padding-block: 1rem .5rem; text-decoration: none; }
  .resource-routes .label { color: var(--home-teal); }
  .resource-title { margin-top: .5rem; font-size: .9375rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .resource-title > span { color: var(--home-teal); }
  .resource-description { margin-top: .5rem; color: var(--home-muted); font-size: .8125rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  .resource-routes a:hover .resource-title { color: var(--home-gold); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: .3em; }
  .archive { border-top: 1px solid var(--home-rule); padding-block: 1.25rem; }
  .course-directory { color: var(--home-muted); font-size: .875rem; }
  .course-directory summary { cursor: pointer; width: fit-content; padding-block: .5rem; color: var(--home-text); }
  .course-directory summary:hover { color: var(--home-gold); }
  .course-directory summary > .label { color: var(--home-teal); margin-inline: .5rem .75rem; }
  .archive-count { color: var(--home-muted); margin-left: .75rem; font: .6875rem/1.5 var(--home-mono); white-space: nowrap; }
  .directory-content { margin-top: 1rem; padding: 1.25rem; border: 1px solid var(--home-rule); background: var(--home-panel); }
  .directory-content h3 { font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--home-text); }
  .article-list, .lesson-list { padding-left: 1.375rem; margin-block: .75rem 1.5rem; }
  .lesson-list { columns: 2 16rem; column-gap: 2rem; }
  .directory-content li { padding-block: .3rem; break-inside: avoid; }
  .directory-content li a { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: .25em; }
  .archive-kind { display: inline-block; color: var(--home-muted); margin-left: .5rem; font: .6875rem/1.5 var(--home-mono); }
  .learning-path-link { color: var(--home-teal); }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .opening { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.625rem; }
    .destination { max-width: 38rem; }
    .connected-systems { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 10rem minmax(0, 1fr); gap: .75rem; }
    .cycle-name { font-size: .75rem; letter-spacing: .02rem; }
    .cycle-node { font-size: .75rem; padding-inline: .25rem; }
    .decision { font-size: .875rem; padding-inline: .5rem; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .connected-systems { grid-template-columns: 1fr; max-width: 22.5rem; margin-inline: auto; gap: .5rem; }
    .decision-hub { margin: .25rem 1.5rem 1rem; }
    .flow-label span { transform: rotate(90deg); }
    .cycle-name { font-size: .8125rem; }
    .cycle-node { font-size: .8125rem; }
    .shared-thread { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: .625rem; }
    .example-thread { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.75rem; }
    .example-step + .example-step { border-top: 1px solid var(--home-rule); padding-top: 1.125rem; }
    .step-connector { display: none; }
    .notes { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.375rem; }
    .note { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.5fr; gap: .5rem 1.5rem; }
    .note-number { grid-column: 1; margin-bottom: 0; }
    .note h2 { grid-column: 1; }
    .note > p:last-child { grid-column: 2; grid-row: 1 / 3; margin-top: 0; }
    .more-reading { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 500px) {
    .opening { padding-block: 2rem; }
    h1 { font-size: 2.125rem; letter-spacing: -.075rem; line-height: 1.13; }
    h1 br { display: none; }
    h1 span { display: block; }
    .kicker { line-height: 1.6; }
    .deck, .principle { font-size: .875rem; }
    .section-heading { flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: .625rem; }
    .section-heading h2 { font-size: 1.5rem; }
    .approach { padding-top: 1.5rem; }
    .example { padding: 1.25rem 1.125rem; }
    figcaption { text-align: left; font-size: .8125rem; }
    .note { display: block; }
    .note-number { margin-bottom: .75rem; }
    .note > p:last-child { margin-top: .9375rem; }
    .resource-routes { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1rem; }
    .archive-count { display: block; margin: .5rem 0 0 1.5rem; }
  }
</style>
